{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 48, :comments ["<b>Blessed.</b> The words of the poet are in prophecy, for the prayer 'Save us, HaShem' — HaShem heard and blessed him concerning the salvation of Israel; then he calls HaShem the Elohim of Israel. And what seems correct to me is that it is joined with praise, then we all say 'Blessed from world to world, He is blessed.'" "<b>And the word amen</b> — from the root אמונה. And he sealed the psalm as he began it, which is the word Hallelujah."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 106, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:38:52.160529026Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}